Description: Battery charge threshold controller for Linux laptops
 Threshold provides a GTK4 graphical interface for setting the
 battery charge threshold on Linux laptops. The charge limit is written
 directly to the EC microcontroller via the msi-ec kernel module and
 persists across reboots.
 .
 Typical use cases include setting a 60–80% charge ceiling to extend
 long-term battery lifespan when the laptop is primarily used plugged in.

Package: msi-ec-dkms
Architecture: amd64
Section: kernel
Depends: dkms (>= 2.2), ${misc:Depends}
Description: MSI Embedded Controller kernel module (DKMS)
 Kernel module that exposes battery charge control and other EC
 features for MSI laptops. Built via DKMS against the running kernel.
 .
 The module registers itself with the Linux power supply subsystem and
 exposes charge_control_start_threshold and charge_control_end_threshold
 under /sys/class/power_supply/BAT*, which threshold writes to.
 .
 Supports EC firmware 16RKIMS1.111 (MSI Thin A15 B7UCX) and other MSI
 laptops supported by upstream msi-ec.
